<%# locals: (f:) %>
<%# The list's search, the third row of the filter panel (Handout §3.4).

    ⚠️ A FIELD of the filter form, not a form of its own. It had its own
    form_tag while it stood outside the panel; inside the panel that would be a
    form inside a form, which does not survive the parser -- the very trap this
    file used to carry a warning about. Making it a field removes the trap
    instead of documenting it: there is now ONE form on this panel, so no
    parameter is emitted twice under the same name and no selector has to guess
    which copy it found. The data-filter-state handles stay, because the ticket
    and meeting ids are still set by LINKS rather than by fields.

    Deliberately wider and whiter than the four choice surfaces above it: it is
    a different gattung and must not read as a fifth chooser.

    auto-submit debounces text inputs (lib/auto_submit.js), so it still answers
    while you type, into time_sessions_list_frame like every other change here.
    The status figures and the reset ride along with that answer (_index_table). %>
<%# min-w-0 max-w-full: this row is a flex item, and a flex item never shrinks
    below its content's minimum on its own. Without them the field's 420px
    held the whole row that wide on a phone, past the drawer's edge; with them
    the field ends at the edge (max-w-full) and keeps 420px wherever it fits. %>
<div class="flex items-center gap-3 flex-wrap min-w-0 max-w-full">
  <%# No fill of its own: from lg up the zone around it is the white filter
      stripe, where a white field would simply disappear. The ring carries the
      field, on the stripe and in the mobile drawer alike. %>
  <div class="flex items-center gap-2.5 w-[420px] max-w-full px-[11px] py-[7px] rounded-lg
              shadow-[inset_0_0_0_1px_theme(colors.cream.400)]
              focus-within:shadow-[inset_0_0_0_1.5px_theme(colors.cream.700)] transition-shadow">
    <i class="bi bi-search text-xs text-cream-700 flex-shrink-0" aria-hidden="true"></i>
    <%= f.search_field :search, value: params[:search],
                       placeholder: t('views.organisations.time_sessions.index.search_placeholder'),
                       autocomplete: 'off',
                       class: 'flex-1 min-w-0 bg-transparent border-0 p-0 text-[13px] text-cream-900 placeholder:text-cream-500 focus:outline-none focus:ring-0',
                       id: 'searchInput',
                       data: { keyboard_navigation_target: 'searchInput', 'time-sessions-index-target': 'searchInput' } %>
    <%# Emptying the field is a filter change like any other, so it is a LINK to
        the address without it -- not a button that clears the input and hopes
        something submits. Works with no JavaScript for the same reason. %>
    <% if params[:search].present? %>
      <%= link_to time_filter_removal_url(:search),
                  data: time_filter_owns(time_filter_owns_pairs(TimeSessionsHelper::TIME_FILTER_REMOVALS.fetch(:search)))
                          .merge(search_clear: true),
                  class: 'flex-shrink-0 text-cream-600 hover:text-cream-900',
                  aria: { label: t('views.organisations.time_sessions.index.search_clear') } do %>
        <i class="bi bi-x-lg text-[11px]" aria-hidden="true"></i>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>
  </div>

  <%= render 'organisations/time_sessions/search_hits' %>
</div>
